# FreeLinX /etc/services - service name to port and transport.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
#
# This file is not optional.  A program that calls getservbyname("ntp") or
# getservbyport() gets ENOENT without it, and FreeLinX's own time daemon is
# such a program:
#
#     src/ntpd.c ... ntp.c:108:   if ((se = getservbyname("ntp", "udp")) == NULL)
#     src/ntpd.c ... ntp.c:109:           fatal("getservbyname");
#
# so with no /etc/services the ntpd service died on start with
#
#     ntp: getservbyname: No such file or directory
#     Terminating
#
# and runsvdir restarted it, about once a second, forever.
#
# musl does not carry a built-in copy of this table: unlike glibc, its resolver
# reads the file and nothing else.  That is the right design for a system whose
# services are its own, and it means the file has to exist.
#
# This is the subset of the IANA registry that FreeLinX itself and the software
# on the medium refer to by name.  It is not the full registry, and it is not
# meant to be: a system that talks to something whose port is not listed here
# can still use the number.  Add a line when a program you install needs one
# that is missing, keeping the three columns aligned.
#
# The authoritative list is at https://www.iana.org/assignments/service-names-port-numbers/

